# Pose manifest for the terrain fill-tag sweep (tests/freecam/fill_sweep.py).
# One pose per line: level | x,y,z,yaw,pitch | tag
#
# Selection rule: canonical-plausible cameras (gameplay-like views, plus the
# validated gapfill/freecam corpus spots). The og legs are only valid ground
# truth where the .s occlusion/culling verdicts fire for cameras the game
# could plausibly have; fully detached orbits under-cover in og and can only
# ADD candidate faces via views the game never shows — the review tier and
# the stencil gate bound that risk, but prefer plausible poses.
#
# Ordering matters for the marginal-new-faces curve: the harness processes
# poses in file order and reports how many new faces each pose contributes,
# per level — the convergence signal that decides sweep density.

